From c641a7a34f7c011e23dd3650ddeec6a1d061df77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:59:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/24] Vizzbox: tuned by measurement (song lengths, the drop,
 the mix, the loudness)

The plan fits the length at the song's tempo: NORMAL 4:45 .. 6:10, SHORT 2:30 .. 3:35 (the middle again,
the calm sections halved; ambient's middle without a DROP). A BUILD's last beat goes silent where the style
has it (else by chance with VARIATION): every track's notes end, the FX layer's FILTER takes what rings on.
The riser is the budget's last to go in a BUILD; a held chord, riser or atmosphere starts a beat later
instead of going. The BUILD's HPF reaches further.

The mix: the role levels from the measurements now keep the drops out of Skiff's master limiter (its gain
reduction about 1 dB on average, was 3..9 dB): each role's loudness lower, each sound's peak alone capped.
VB_TRIM (tools/vizzbox_level.py) brings the subgenres' demos to one loudness.

tools/vizzbox_render: the boot no longer in the WAV (it ran 0.6 s behind the MIDI file); prints the key's
scale and the six sounds. tools/vizzbox_demos.py: every subgenre rendered, its part from a BUILD into the
DROP as MP3, the whole song's MIDI file, and the checks of BRIEF 8 (clipping, loudness, notes outside the
key, sections, kick on bass, the jump into the drop, the silence before it, the riser).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R1rawnvCsrvDZVbc37ZFUY
